In modern engineering, speed means nothing without stability. Here's how I approach DevOps at scale — from planning epics to monitoring production — using battle-tested tools across each phase:
🔸 𝗣𝗟𝗔𝗡 → Define SLAs, user stories, and architecture with tools like Jira.
 🔸 𝗗𝗘𝗩𝗘𝗟𝗢𝗣 → Version control and collaboration via GitHub.
 🔸 𝗕𝗨𝗜𝗟𝗗 → CI pipelines powered by Jenkins for automated packaging.
 🔸 𝗧𝗘𝗦𝗧 → Functional and security validation using Selenium and SonarQube.
 🔸 𝗥𝗘𝗟𝗘𝗔𝗦𝗘 → Helm charts and Git tagging for version readiness.
 🔸 𝗗𝗘𝗣𝗟𝗢𝗬 → ArgoCD and Terraform for GitOps-driven environment sync.
 🔸 𝗢𝗣𝗘𝗥𝗔𝗧𝗘 → Kubernetes and cloud platforms ensure uptime and scalability.
 🔸 𝗠𝗢𝗡𝗜𝗧𝗢𝗥 → Prometheus and Grafana for full-stack observability.
This isn’t just a workflow — it’s a mindset. Every stage is engineered for reliability, velocity, and visibility.
 Whether you're scaling multi-cloud infrastructure or optimizing delivery pipelines, this lifecycle is the backbone of resilient systems.
